    {
      "text": "by thy words thou shalt be condemned, Matt. 12:37. The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it, Matt. 12:41 (Luke 11:32). they shall condemn him to death, Matt. 20:18 (Mark 10:33; 14:64). condemn not, and ye shall not be condemned, Luke 6:37. God sent not his Son into the world to condemn, John 3:17. Neither do I condemn thee: go, and sin no more, John 8:11. God sending his own Son … for sin, condemned sin in the flesh, Rom. 8:3. chastened … that we should not be condemned with the world, 1 Cor. 11:32. he … is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself, Titus 3:11. prepared an ark … he condemned the world, Heb. 11:7. Grudge not … lest ye be condemned, James 5:9. if our heart condemn us, 1 Jn. 3:20.",
